  "featured_image_url": "https://thedrakelawfirm.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/you-got-divorced-now-what.png",
  "content": {
    "rendered": "<p>Divorce can be the most stressful and upsetting time in a person’s life. Here at the Drake Law Firm, we believe in helping people divorce with as little drama possible. However, that does not change the fact that divorce is hurtful and can be hard to accept. Below are a few tips on how to move forward after divorce.</p>\n<h2>Ask for Help</h2>\n<p>Divorce comes with many life changes. Do not be afraid to ask your support system for help. Friends and family members are empathizing with you, and it is important to remember you are not alone. Therapy is another great tool to utilize. Self-care is incredibly important on the journey after divorce.</p>\n<h2>Let the Kids be Kids</h2>\n<p>Leave the kids out of the drama. Divorce is a big life change for your children as is.</p>\n<p>They are likely hurting or confused already and do not need to worry about the adult specifics of divorce. Make sure that they know they are loved by both parents and take the time to show them some extra care.</p>\n<h2>Look Ahead</h2>\n<p>It is important to accept the reality of divorce and look ahead. There may be feelings of anger or resentment. Acknowledge these feelings and let yourself heal to move forward. While it may be scary, there is a new life awaiting you. Think of all of the good that is to come.</p>\n<h2>Contact the Drake Law Firm Today</h2>\n<p>If you are ready to move forward with your divorce, contact us at the <a href=\"https://thedrakelawfirm.com/\">Drake Law Firm</a> today by giving us a call at <a href=\"tel:303-261-8111\">303-261-8111</a>.</p>\n"
  },
